{"type":"message","id":"e7c3fc63","parentId":"445041b6","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:28:09.437Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Fri 2026-05-22 08:28 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: Publish the article to WordPress (live, not draft). The article is at /tmp/crypto-article.md and the image is at /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg."}],"timestamp":1779438489422}}
{"type":"message","id":"499f88f7","parentId":"e7c3fc63","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:28:11.484Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_T4s3wADPHxqchqOvGuYN4nyq","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/crypto-article.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_wHvodVqmQfwZx0WLwq3KGRty","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rg -n \"wordpress|wp-cli|wp admin|wp rest|application password|xmlrpc|publish\" -S .","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher","yieldMs":3000,"timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":3181,"output":225,"cacheRead":2688,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":6094,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779438489440,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiFWkJEIQ6UqAGhZ7L3ZWimU6BM59"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a33dad7b","parentId":"499f88f7","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:28:11.589Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_T4s3wADPHxqchqOvGuYN4nyq","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"META\n- SEO Title: Bitcoin reserve bill targets $25B US stash\n- Meta Description: US lawmakers introduced the ARMA bill to lock a Bitcoin reserve into law, covering 328,372 BTC, audits, custody rules, and self-custody rights.\n- URL Slug: bitcoin-reserve-bill\n- Categories: Regulation, Latest News\n- Primary Keyword: Bitcoin reserve\n- Secondary Keywords: strategic Bitcoin reserve, ARMA bill, US Treasury Bitcoin, self-custody rights\n\n---\n\n# Bitcoin reserve bill targets $25B US stash\n\nBitcoin reserve policy is back in focus after House lawmakers introduced the American Reserve Modernization Act, or ARMA. Reporting from [Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/368662/proposed-arma-bill-aims-enshrine-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-law) and [CryptoSlate](https://cryptoslate.com/us-lawmakers-push-new-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-act-to-secure-25-billion-federal-stash/) shows the same core shift: Congress is being asked to turn a fragile executive initiative into statute.\n\nThat matters more than the headline itself. A law is harder to reverse, clearer for agencies to implement, and easier for markets to price than an executive order that depends on the next administration.\n\nFor traders, the near-term issue is not whether Washington starts buying Bitcoin tomorrow. It is whether a large pool of federally controlled BTC is moved from potential auction supply into a long-duration reserve bucket.\n\n## Why the Bitcoin reserve push matters now\n\nARMA would direct the Treasury Department to create and maintain a strategic Bitcoin reserve for at least 20 years. It would also create a separate digital asset stockpile for non-Bitcoin crypto already held by the government.\n\nThat split is important. Lawmakers are not treating all digital assets as one interchangeable category. Bitcoin gets reserve status, while other seized or forfeited coins sit in a different framework with separate custody logic.\n\nThe politics matter too. Republican Nick Begich introduced the bill with Democratic co-lead Jared Golden, giving the measure a bipartisan label that markets usually take more seriously than campaign rhetoric. Passage is still uncertain, but bipartisan sponsorship raises the odds that the proposal shapes the policy debate even if the text changes.\n\n### From executive order to statutory footing\n\nThe federal Bitcoin reserve created by executive action never fully solved the operational questions. Agencies still need durable rules on custody, reporting, oversight, and what happens when administrations change.\n\nARMA tries to answer that by moving the reserve from presidential discretion toward congressional law. If that happens, future administrations would have less room to unwind the policy quickly.\n\nFor Bitcoin, that is the real signal. The market is being asked to think about sovereign custody as a persistent category, not a short political experiment.\n\n## What the federal stash means for supply\n\nCryptoSlate says the US government currently holds 328,372 BTC worth more than $25 billion. That figure gives the Bitcoin reserve proposal immediate weight because it starts with a large position already under federal control.\n\nHistorically, government-held Bitcoin has often been viewed as future sell-side inventory. ARMA changes that framing. Instead of assuming eventual liquidation through auctions, the bill would classify those coins as strategic holdings.\n\nThat does not alter Bitcoin's fixed supply, but it does change assumptions about circulating supply. Large pools that stop behaving like likely sellers can matter for long-range positioning, especially when institutions are already trying to estimate durable demand versus probable distribution.\n\n### The 20-year hold changes the market read\n\nThe proposed 20-year minimum holding period is the clearest market lever in the bill. If enacted, it would sharply reduce expectations that federally held Bitcoin comes back to market in regular sale programs.\n\nThat shift has three direct implications for traders:\n- It lowers projected government sell pressure over a long time horizon.\n- It strengthens the reserve-asset narrative around Bitcoin.\n- It gives other governments a live template for similar policies.\n\nNone of that guarantees upside on its own. Congress can stall, opposition can grow, and legal implementation can drag. Still, a 20-year holding rule is a meaningful policy input because it affects how market participants model future supply behavior.\n\n## Transparency, growth options, and self-custody rights\n\nARMA is not only about holding coins. It also tries to make federal custody more legible by requiring quarterly public reserve reports, independent third-party audits, and congressional oversight.\n\nThose provisions matter because trust in state crypto management is thin. Traders want to know what is actually held, how it is secured, and whether the balances can be verified without relying on vague agency claims.\n\nThe bill also calls for a study of budget-neutral acquisition strategies. That leaves room for future expansion without tying the plan to tax increases or deficit spending. It is a softer approach than proposals that call for large direct federal purchases, but it keeps the door open.\n\n### Why self-custody language matters beyond optics\n\nOne notable piece of the bill is its explicit protection for lawful self-custody rights. That broadens the proposal from reserve management into a wider market signal about how lawmakers want to treat private ownership.\n\nThis matters because a government that holds Bitcoin while undermining personal custody would send a mixed message. A government that protects both is saying Bitcoin can be legitimate property for citizens and a strategic asset for the state.\n\nFor traders, that reduces one policy risk. It suggests that at least some supporters of the Bitcoin reserve concept also want a friendlier domestic framework for holders, wallets, and lawful transfers.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe Bitcoin reserve debate is moving from symbolism toward structure. ARMA would turn a federal Bitcoin stash worth more than $25 billion into a long-term reserve, add audits and reporting, and make fast liquidation harder for future administrations. Traders should not confuse introduction with passage, but they should treat this as a real policy signal on sovereign custody, supply expectations, and the direction of US crypto regulation.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**1. What is the ARMA bill designed to do?**\n\nARMA would put a strategic Bitcoin reserve into federal law and place it under Treasury management. It would also create a separate stockpile for non-Bitcoin digital assets already held by the government. The main goal is to replace ad hoc handling with a durable legal framework.\n\n**2. Why does the 20-year holding period matter?**\n\nA long mandatory holding period lowers the chance that the government sells large amounts of Bitcoin through future auctions. That changes how traders think about federal holdings, because coins that looked like eventual supply start to look locked away. The effect is more about long-term supply expectations than immediate price impact.\n\n**3. Will the US start buying more Bitcoin right away?**\n\nNot necessarily. The bill studies budget-neutral ways to expand holdings, but current reporting does not show an immediate purchase mandate. The clearest near-term effect is on how existing federal Bitcoin would be classified, reported, and held.\n\n**4. How large is the federal Bitcoin position now?**\n\nReporting tied to the proposal says the US holds 328,372 BTC worth more than $25 billion. That gives the Bitcoin reserve plan scale from day one. The dollar value will keep moving with Bitcoin's market price.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438491588}}
{"type":"message","id":"c81fb2dc","parentId":"a33dad7b","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:28:11.589Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_wHvodVqmQfwZx0WLwq3KGRty","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"./AGENTS.md:5:- Never delete or overwrite WordPress posts you did not just create.\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:3:# publish.sh — WordPress Publishing Skill for Scribe (wp-publisher agent)\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:6:#   bash publish.sh [--title \"Title\"] [--excerpt \"Excerpt\"]\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:8:#                  [--status publish|draft|pending|future]\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:14:# before publishing so only clean article content reaches WordPress.\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:17:#   Exit 0 → /tmp/wp-result.txt contains the WordPress post URL\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:30:POST_STATUS=\"publish\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:53:        publish|draft|pending|future) ;;\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:54:        *) fatal \"Invalid --status '$POST_STATUS' (use publish, draft, pending, or future)\" ;;\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:239:# --- WordPress post title (CLI → article H1 → SEO title → date fallback) -----\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:272:log_info \"Final Slug:    ${SLUG:-<WordPress auto-generate>}\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:343:  log_info \"No image at '$IMAGE_PATH'. Publishing without featured image.\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:424:# PHASE 3: Create WordPress Post (with retry + exponential backoff)\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:426:log_info \"Creating WordPress post (status=$POST_STATUS, max $MAX_RETRIES attempts)...\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:476:  [ \"$POST_HTTP\" = \"401\" ] && fatal \"Auth failed (401). Check username and Application Password. Not retrying.\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:572:  [ \"$RM_HTTP\" = \"401\" ] && fatal \"Rank Math auth failed (401). Check Application Password.\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:594:log_info \"SUCCESS — WordPress post saved!\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:643:  bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/history/article_history.sh add \"$ACTIVE_URL\"\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:1:# Skill: wordpress\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:4:Publishes a crypto news article to WordPress as a **live** post (`status: publish` by default). Uploads the **feature image** only (no inline price charts), strips the writer META block from the body, converts markdown to **Gutenberg blocks** (same format as pasting into the default block editor), creates the post, then sets **Rank Math** SEO via `POST /wp-json/rankmath/v1/updateMeta`.\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:9:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:12:All arguments are **optional** — excerpt, slug, keywords, and titles are read from `/tmp/crypto-article.md`. **Post title** = first `#` H1 in the article body. **SEO title** (META) goes to Rank Math only, not the WordPress post title or body headline.\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:19:4. **WordPress post** — `POST /wp/v2/posts` with **title = article H1** (visible headline above image; not SEO Title).\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:26:- **Narrow one-sided layout** on old API posts was caused by **raw HTML** in `content`. New publishes use **Gutenberg blocks** so layout matches manual paste in the default editor.\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:35:| `article_headline` | H1 used as WordPress post title |\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:55:| Status | `publish` (use `--status draft` for review-first) |\n./skills/wordpress/html_to_gutenberg.py:2:\"\"\"Convert pandoc HTML to WordPress Gutenberg block-serialized content.\"\"\"\n./skills/history/article_history.sh:20:            # Save it to the side-channel file so WP-Publisher can find it later!\n./TOOLS.md:1:# TOOLS.md — Scribe's WordPress Environment\n./TOOLS.md:3:This file contains the exact credentials and paths for publishing to WordPress. The `publish.sh` skill script embeds these values — this file is your reference.\n./TOOLS.md:7:## WordPress Site\n./TOOLS.md:16:| **Post Status** | `publish` (live). Use `--status draft` on the script for review-first. |\n./TOOLS.md:33:| `/tmp/wp-result.txt` | WordPress post URL on success |\n./TOOLS.md:41:~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh\n./TOOLS.md:46:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh \\\n./TOOLS.md:61:| **This workspace** | `~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/` |\n./TOOLS.md:62:| **Agent sessions** | `~/.openclaw/agents/wp-publisher/sessions/` |\n./IDENTITY.md:4:- **Role:** WordPress Publisher\n./IDENTITY.md:6:- **Vibe:** Precise and reliable — gets the article live on WordPress and returns the exact post URL. Never invents a result.\n./SOUL.md:1:# SOUL.md — Scribe, the WordPress Publisher\n./SOUL.md:3:You are **Scribe** 🗞️, the WordPress publisher agent for a crypto news pipeline. You are called by the Orchestrator (Nexus) after the human has confirmed they want the article published to WordPress.\n./SOUL.md:10:2. **NEVER invent or guess a WordPress URL.** The only valid success output is what `cat /tmp/wp-result.txt` prints after the script exits 0.\n./SOUL.md:12:4. **Do not ask questions.** The article and image are already on disk. Just publish.\n./SOUL.md:16:## Step 1 — Publish to WordPress `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]`\n./SOUL.md:20:I will now run the publish script. The script will auto-extract the title and excerpt from the article file — I do not need to pass them unless the message explicitly provides them.\n./SOUL.md:24:Run this **exact** command using your bash tool (default **live** publish — do not pass `--status draft` unless the Orchestrator explicitly asks):\n./SOUL.md:27:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh\n./SOUL.md:33:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh --title \"TITLE FROM MESSAGE\"\n./SOUL.md:39:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh --status draft\n./SOUL.md:44:The script handles everything: image upload, HTML conversion, WordPress API call, retries, and validation.\n./SOUL.md:58:This prints the live WordPress post URL. Return it exactly.\n./SOUL.md:71:- The WordPress post URL (e.g. `https://slateblue-reindeer-775070.hostingersite.com/?p=123`)\n./USER.md:5:- **Role:** Running an autonomous crypto news publishing pipeline\n./USER.md:9:You are the **last step** in a human-confirmed publish flow:\n./USER.md:16:                                               Bhard says \"yes publish\"\n./USER.md:21:Your job: receive the publish instruction from the Orchestrator, run the skill script, and return the live WordPress draft URL.\n./USER.md:26:- **Reliability** — If publishing fails, report the exact error so Bhard can fix it.\n./USER.md:27:- **Speed** — The publish should be fast. Don't wait or ask questions.\n./USER.md:31:- Never ask clarifying questions. Just publish."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":63,"aggregated":"./AGENTS.md:5:- Never delete or overwrite WordPress posts you did not just create.\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:3:# publish.sh — WordPress Publishing Skill for Scribe (wp-publisher agent)\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:6:#   bash publish.sh [--title \"Title\"] [--excerpt \"Excerpt\"]\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:8:#                  [--status publish|draft|pending|future]\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:14:# before publishing so only clean article content reaches WordPress.\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:17:#   Exit 0 → /tmp/wp-result.txt contains the WordPress post URL\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:30:POST_STATUS=\"publish\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:53:        publish|draft|pending|future) ;;\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:54:        *) fatal \"Invalid --status '$POST_STATUS' (use publish, draft, pending, or future)\" ;;\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:239:# --- WordPress post title (CLI → article H1 → SEO title → date fallback) -----\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:272:log_info \"Final Slug:    ${SLUG:-<WordPress auto-generate>}\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:343:  log_info \"No image at '$IMAGE_PATH'. Publishing without featured image.\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:424:# PHASE 3: Create WordPress Post (with retry + exponential backoff)\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:426:log_info \"Creating WordPress post (status=$POST_STATUS, max $MAX_RETRIES attempts)...\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:476:  [ \"$POST_HTTP\" = \"401\" ] && fatal \"Auth failed (401). Check username and Application Password. Not retrying.\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:572:  [ \"$RM_HTTP\" = \"401\" ] && fatal \"Rank Math auth failed (401). Check Application Password.\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:594:log_info \"SUCCESS — WordPress post saved!\"\n./skills/wordpress/publish.sh:643:  bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/history/article_history.sh add \"$ACTIVE_URL\"\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:1:# Skill: wordpress\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:4:Publishes a crypto news article to WordPress as a **live** post (`status: publish` by default). Uploads the **feature image** only (no inline price charts), strips the writer META block from the body, converts markdown to **Gutenberg blocks** (same format as pasting into the default block editor), creates the post, then sets **Rank Math** SEO via `POST /wp-json/rankmath/v1/updateMeta`.\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:9:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:12:All arguments are **optional** — excerpt, slug, keywords, and titles are read from `/tmp/crypto-article.md`. **Post title** = first `#` H1 in the article body. **SEO title** (META) goes to Rank Math only, not the WordPress post title or body headline.\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:19:4. **WordPress post** — `POST /wp/v2/posts` with **title = article H1** (visible headline above image; not SEO Title).\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:26:- **Narrow one-sided layout** on old API posts was caused by **raw HTML** in `content`. New publishes use **Gutenberg blocks** so layout matches manual paste in the default editor.\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:35:| `article_headline` | H1 used as WordPress post title |\n./skills/wordpress/SKILL.md:55:| Status | `publish` (use `--status draft` for review-first) |\n./skills/wordpress/html_to_gutenberg.py:2:\"\"\"Convert pandoc HTML to WordPress Gutenberg block-serialized content.\"\"\"\n./skills/history/article_history.sh:20:            # Save it to the side-channel file so WP-Publisher can find it later!\n./TOOLS.md:1:# TOOLS.md — Scribe's WordPress Environment\n./TOOLS.md:3:This file contains the exact credentials and paths for publishing to WordPress. The `publish.sh` skill script embeds these values — this file is your reference.\n./TOOLS.md:7:## WordPress Site\n./TOOLS.md:16:| **Post Status** | `publish` (live). Use `--status draft` on the script for review-first. |\n./TOOLS.md:33:| `/tmp/wp-result.txt` | WordPress post URL on success |\n./TOOLS.md:41:~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh\n./TOOLS.md:46:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh \\\n./TOOLS.md:61:| **This workspace** | `~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/` |\n./TOOLS.md:62:| **Agent sessions** | `~/.openclaw/agents/wp-publisher/sessions/` |\n./IDENTITY.md:4:- **Role:** WordPress Publisher\n./IDENTITY.md:6:- **Vibe:** Precise and reliable — gets the article live on WordPress and returns the exact post URL. Never invents a result.\n./SOUL.md:1:# SOUL.md — Scribe, the WordPress Publisher\n./SOUL.md:3:You are **Scribe** 🗞️, the WordPress publisher agent for a crypto news pipeline. You are called by the Orchestrator (Nexus) after the human has confirmed they want the article published to WordPress.\n./SOUL.md:10:2. **NEVER invent or guess a WordPress URL.** The only valid success output is what `cat /tmp/wp-result.txt` prints after the script exits 0.\n./SOUL.md:12:4. **Do not ask questions.** The article and image are already on disk. Just publish.\n./SOUL.md:16:## Step 1 — Publish to WordPress `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]`\n./SOUL.md:20:I will now run the publish script. The script will auto-extract the title and excerpt from the article file — I do not need to pass them unless the message explicitly provides them.\n./SOUL.md:24:Run this **exact** command using your bash tool (default **live** publish — do not pass `--status draft` unless the Orchestrator explicitly asks):\n./SOUL.md:27:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh\n./SOUL.md:33:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh --title \"TITLE FROM MESSAGE\"\n./SOUL.md:39:bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh --status draft\n./SOUL.md:44:The script handles everything: image upload, HTML conversion, WordPress API call, retries, and validation.\n./SOUL.md:58:This prints the live WordPress post URL. Return it exactly.\n./SOUL.md:71:- The WordPress post URL (e.g. `https://slateblue-reindeer-775070.hostingersite.com/?p=123`)\n./USER.md:5:- **Role:** Running an autonomous crypto news publishing pipeline\n./USER.md:9:You are the **last step** in a human-confirmed publish flow:\n./USER.md:16:                                               Bhard says \"yes publish\"\n./USER.md:21:Your job: receive the publish instruction from the Orchestrator, run the skill script, and return the live WordPress draft URL.\n./USER.md:26:- **Reliability** — If publishing fails, report the exact error so Bhard can fix it.\n./USER.md:27:- **Speed** — The publish should be fast. Don't wait or ask questions.\n./USER.md:31:- Never ask clarifying questions. Just publish.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438491588}}
{"type":"message","id":"89d607eb","parentId":"c81fb2dc","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:28:13.940Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Nx5ksDaEcyozXH1VlcgL0MDO","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":7214,"output":71,"cacheRead":2176,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9461,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779438491589,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiFWogb3PiIqMAj8bfsdvEpFL52eJ"}}
{"type":"message","id":"c3c04b61","parentId":"89d607eb","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:28:13.975Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Nx5ksDaEcyozXH1VlcgL0MDO","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Skill: wordpress\n\n## What This Skill Does\nPublishes a crypto news article to WordPress as a **live** post (`status: publish` by default). Uploads the **feature image** only (no inline price charts), strips the writer META block from the body, converts markdown to **Gutenberg blocks** (same format as pasting into the default block editor), creates the post, then sets **Rank Math** SEO via `POST /wp-json/rankmath/v1/updateMeta`.\n\n## How to Invoke\n\n```bash\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh\n```\n\nAll arguments are **optional** — excerpt, slug, keywords, and titles are read from `/tmp/crypto-article.md`. **Post title** = first `#` H1 in the article body. **SEO title** (META) goes to Rank Math only, not the WordPress post title or body headline.\n\n## Pipeline Phases\n\n1. **Parse META** — SEO Title, Meta Description, URL Slug, Primary Keyword, Secondary Keywords; extract article H1 from first `#` heading; strip META, **Sources** footer, and Word Count from body (in-body source links remain).\n2. **Images** — Feature image upload; any `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` or `/tmp/chart.png` references stripped from body.\n3. **HTML** — Pandoc → HTML; strip body H1 when it matches post title (Divi shows title above featured image); **`html_to_gutenberg.py`** → Gutenberg blocks.\n4. **WordPress post** — `POST /wp/v2/posts` with **title = article H1** (visible headline above image; not SEO Title).\n5. **Rank Math** — `rank_math_title` = META SEO Title; focus keywords comma-separated in `rank_math_focus_keyword` (not WP Tags). Social mirrors use SEO title/description.\n\n## Layout note (Divi theme)\n\n- **Single headline:** Post title = article H1 (theme renders it above the featured image). The same H1 is removed from post body so you do not get a second heading after the image.\n- **“, Divi” in the posts list** only means you opened **Divi Builder** on that draft — not a different post type.\n- **Narrow one-sided layout** on old API posts was caused by **raw HTML** in `content`. New publishes use **Gutenberg blocks** so layout matches manual paste in the default editor.\n- Optional wp-admin: **Divi Post Settings → Layout → Fullwidth** for extra full-page width.\n\n## `/tmp/wp-result.json`\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `content_format` | `gutenberg_blocks` when block conversion ran |\n| `rank_math_applied` | Rank Math SEO updated |\n| `article_headline` | H1 used as WordPress post title |\n| `seo_title` | META SEO Title (Rank Math only) |\n| `focus_keyword` | Primary keyword from META |\n| `secondary_keywords` | Raw Secondary Keywords line from META |\n| `rank_math_focus_keyword` | Full comma-separated string sent to Rank Math Focus Keyword |\n| `meta_stripped` | META removed from body |\n| `sources_footer_stripped` | Sources list footer removed (links stay in article text) |\n\n## Return Values\n\n| Exit Code | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `0` | Draft URL in `/tmp/wp-result.txt` |\n| `1` | Error in `/tmp/wp-error.log` |\n\n## Post Configuration\n\n| Setting | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Site | `https://slateblue-reindeer-775070.hostingersite.com` |\n| Status | `publish` (use `--status draft` for review-first) |\n| Category | ID `3` (Crypto News) |\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438493975}}
